### Welcome to SEDS Sabra

SEDS Sabra is the student space chapter at Sabaragamuwa University of Sri Lanka (SUSL), situated in the picturesque surroundings of Belihuloya. Leveraging one of the best dark-sky locations in Sri Lanka, our chapter is famous for immersive stargazing, astronomical exploration, and geospatial science.

### What We Do

SEDS Sabra members take advantage of the natural high-altitude vantage point in Belihuloya:

- **Dark-Sky Astronomical Camps**: Organizing night-sky observation camps with optical telescopes to photograph the Milky Way, star clusters, nebulae, and passing satellites with minimal light pollution.
- **Geoinformatics and Remote Sensing**: Collaborating with students in surveying and geospatial sciences to interpret satellite imagery, land cover maps, and atmospheric data.
- **School Science Outreach**: Traveling to rural schools in the Rathnapura and Balangoda regions to conduct telescope viewing nights and inspire young students with the wonders of the universe.
- **Space Science Discussions**: Hosting campus workshops on telescope optics, basic orbital mechanics, and astrophotography techniques.

### Connect With SEDS Sabra

Every registered student at Sabaragamuwa University of Sri Lanka is welcome to join our activities and night observation sessions.

- **Location**: Sabaragamuwa University of Sri Lanka, Belihuloya.
- **Email**: [sedssabra@sedssl.org](mailto:sedssabra@sedssl.org)
